Each component carries its own licence text inside the package that ships it (the built worker image keeps every bundled package's LICENSE file), and plugins/THIRD_PARTY.md lists the bundled npm packages with their licences.
Every redistributed component keeps its own licence; nothing in the MIT
licence of Phone DSH re-licenses them.

The Android local Ubuntu slice additionally fetches third-party pieces that are
never committed to this repository and never shipped in this repository's
source tree. The build-time proot stack is downloaded by
`android/tools/fetch-termux-proot.sh` from the official Termux package host;
the Ubuntu Base rootfs is downloaded on demand by the Android app itself from
the official Ubuntu image host, after the user approves the first `ubuntu run`.

