Google Play's executable-code policy may treat the on-demand rootfs
download as restricted; this repository's slice is for sideload/development
builds until that question is decided. The app never downloads an arbitrary
URL: the URL, size and SHA-256 are pinned in
`android/platform-android/.../UbuntuRootfsStore.kt`.

Artwork: the mascot in docs/assets/logo.png, the community QR image
(docs/assets/qq-group-714985308.png) and the app icon are fan artwork
of the DeepSeek assistant character, included as project branding. They are
not covered by the MIT licence of the source code and are not official
DeepSeek assets.

The Android app's native SSH/SCP accelerator (docs/native-ssh.md) links two
Maven Central libraries, pinned in android/gradle/libs.versions.toml:

  - JSch 2.28.8 (com.github.mwiede:jsch)     BSD-3-Clause (JSch, JZlib) and
    ISC (jBCrypt); https://github.com/mwiede/jsch
  - Bouncy Castle bcprov-jdk18on 1.86        MIT-style Bouncy Castle Licence;
    https://www.bouncycastle.org/licence.html

PDSH BLE Home Bridge includes the MIT-licensed policy, bounded TCP transport,
legacy control vectors, and related tests identified by
firmware/components/pdsh_home/vendor/UPSTREAM.json. The original license and
copyright notice are retained in that vendor directory.
